1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
To be continued...

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Come on, sister! Stay with us!

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Old Hag, wake up! You can't die on me!

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
If you keeled over now, Marie would be sad.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
And I... wouldn't be too happy about it either.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Take... take care of them.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The children...

11
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
It's always the same.

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
No matter who wins on any battlefield, it's the weak who pay the greatest price.

13
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Children are innocent, untouched by sin.

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
They were the ones I most wanted to protect.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
And so I left the battlefield behind, and devoted myself to the church.

16
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Sister!

17
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
What kind of nonsense is that?

18
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
No one is pure. You're all tainted by sin from the moment of your birth.

19
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
You're insane!

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Just look at you, Sally. Poor thing. They've hurt you so badly.

21
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
I tried, Master.

22
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
You did well, but now it's time for you to rest.

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Valtos...

24
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Yes, sir.

25
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,000
To be continued...

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
That's a deal.

27
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
To be continued...

28
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,000
To be continued...

29
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Bye, Asta. Catch you later.

30
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Don't forget, Precious.

31
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,000
You belong to me.

32
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Please just leave me alone!

33
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:15,400
i'm to blame for this i should never have sent her here by herself this outcome was unexpected

34
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:21,480
you needn't feel responsible for what happened we all know how they fight

35
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:26,680
no doubt they resorted to underhanded tactics you're saying that we fight dirty after what

36
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:33,560
that crazy lackey of yours did to those poor kids you know the sister was wrong before

37
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:40,520
it isn't the weak who pay not at all it is the strong who have been victimized

38
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:52,760
feared discriminated against persecuted and stolen from what's he talking about that's crazy

39
00:02:53,560 --> 00:03:01,160
for its crimes the clover kingdom cannot be forgiven instead we will destroy you as you so richly

40
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:07,240
deserve and build a nation of our own where do you get off acting like we're the bad guys here

41
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:10,760
you and your group of psychos started all this you jerk

42
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:22,680
i refuse to listen to that kind of filth it's painful really seeing someone as disgusting as you

43
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:29,160
with that grimoire my grimoire never mind i need to stay focused on his attacks

44
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:34,200
they come so fast i can't even see them what do i do

45
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:40,760
the only thing i can do use my sword as a shield to block any fatal blows

46
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:50,760
i'm not dying yes you are i'll just be taking that grimoire back from you now

47
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:53,160
this is it

48
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:55,880
i'm dead

49
00:03:55,880 --> 00:04:01,960
no way

50
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:07,400
captain yummy what are you doing here

51
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:23,880
why am i here well hell kid i guess i must have gotten lost anybody know where the bar is

52
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:27,880
what are you doing here

53
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:46,360
oh

54
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:47,640
in

55
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,060
What's your face for you?

56
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:51,500
水平線が中央魔王

57
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,960
何度挫かれても

58
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:58,060
その希望を両手に

59
00:04:58,060 --> 00:05:00,360
僕ら波を打って

60
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,640
ツバッシャーを

61
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:07,320
シーセローと叫ぶんだ

62
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:08,580
Get down!

63
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:10,200
We all let you down!

64
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:10,920
Best one!

65
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:12,540
Can you bring me down?

66
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,240
Back up!

67
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:15,340
Get far out of the sky!

68
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,040
Black Clover!

69
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:19,040
いつか共に

70
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:21,940
火を今は黒に染めよう

71
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:24,900
こんなふざけた時代

72
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:26,740
Black Clover!

73
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:28,640
今日の間に

74
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:30,940
僕ら並べたって

75
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:33,140
今から

76
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:35,540
扉を

77
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:38,440
開くから

78
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:44,740
Let's go!

79
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:57,300
これが

80
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:59,240
Got rocks in there instead of brains?

81
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:01,320
That's what people call a joke.

82
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:02,000
What?

83
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:05,160
I'm a magic knight and there's trouble.

84
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,940
That's what I'm doing here, idiot.

85
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:10,360
We heard about what was going on,

86
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:13,280
but everyone back at the hideout was useless as usual,

87
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:14,340
so here I am.

88
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:15,920
I'll kill them all later.

89
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:18,400
They couldn't pull it together this once?!

90
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:21,020
This is why we're here?

91
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:22,920
I wish he'd just let me sleep.

92
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,180
What the hell are you doing anyway?

93
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:27,180
I gave all you knuckleheads the day off.

94
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:29,880
Maybe what you need is a more permanent vacation.

95
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:37,240
So, what's up with this guy?

96
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:40,280
He says he's the leader of the Hive and Midnight Sun.

97
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:42,840
No way! Not them again!

98
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:43,560
Oh yeah?

99
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,420
Here I've been picturing a super buff guy

100
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:49,300
who ate cows whole or something.

101
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:51,660
Not some scrawny freak.

102
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:55,600
Not everything in this world is about muscles.

103
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:59,140
This guy has magic power practically pouring out of him.

104
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,200
It's bottomless.

105
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:01,940
And light magic?

106
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:03,620
That's super rare stuff.

107
00:07:03,980 --> 00:07:07,100
Only a few people in the whole history of the Clover Kingdom have ever wielded it.

108
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:10,720
Whatever happens next, it isn't going to be pretty.

109
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:12,440
I want to go home.

110
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:16,360
So, the Black Bull's captain came himself.

111
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,680
Shall I summon the Third Eye now?

112
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:19,680
No need.

113
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:22,740
You see, the captain here is a wielder of dark magic.

114
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,740
I'll enjoy pitting my power against his in battle.

115
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:27,960
Hey, Finral.

116
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,820
Can you get the others to the village?

117
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,400
Sure, leave it to me.

118
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:32,680
But what about you?

119
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:36,840
I can still fight!

120
00:07:38,340 --> 00:07:40,900
This is my chance to see Captain Yami in action.

121
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:42,500
No way am I leaving now!

122
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:45,440
Gosh, and...

123
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:47,440
Well, whoever you are, can you walk?

124
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:49,080
Shooter the old hag first!

125
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:49,840
And hurry!

126
00:07:50,020 --> 00:07:50,820
Right, got it!

127
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:54,180
Never mind that I'm actually your superior.

128
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:56,360
Alright, Captain.

129
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,100
It's up to you now.

130
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:01,300
Hey, you better be coming back.

131
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:04,140
Did he know I was planning to sneak off?

132
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:05,260
He couldn't, right?

133
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:09,380
Well, you know, I think I might be a little low on Mana.

134
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:11,540
So, really, I'm not kidding!

135
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:12,100
Yeah?

136
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:13,300
Look at my face.

137
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:14,940
Does it look like I'm kidding?

138
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:16,720
No, sir.

139
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:18,180
I guess it doesn't.

140
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:25,020
Are you trying to mess up my ride or something?

141
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:26,160
His ride?

142
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:28,740
All right, time to get out of here.

143
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,500
I'm not looking to die today.

144
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,260
I'm off!

145
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,880
Gotta get these people to safety!

146
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:36,480
You better be coming back, you hear me, Finral?

147
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:37,560
So cool!

148
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,640
How'd you know that strike was coming?

149
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:41,540
What kind of sword is that?

150
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:42,320
Where'd you get him?

151
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:43,300
Shut up, would ya?

152
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:46,400
This is a katana.

153
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:48,980
It's from my native country, the Land of the Sun.

154
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,660
I blocked his hit by...

155
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:51,420
Oh, never mind.

156
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:52,680
No time to explain.

157
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:54,540
Besides, it's boring that way.

158
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:55,620
Just watch.

159
00:08:56,180 --> 00:08:57,620
Engage light magic.

160
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,780
Light swords of conviction.

161
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:03,480
Awesome!

162
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:12,440
He's using reinforcement magic to boost his natural abilities and cloaking his sword in dark magic to slice through my spell.

163
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:17,240
Except, there's more to it than that.

164
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:19,540
Very well.

165
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:21,460
Let's try something else, then.

166
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:27,820
Impressive.

167
00:09:27,820 --> 00:09:30,940
The power of an unorthodox grand magic knight.

168
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:32,260
Hold on.

169
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:32,980
You know?

170
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:35,740
I think I recognize you from somewhere.

171
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:46,440
Except I'm pretty sure I'd remember if I knew somebody who could use light magic.

172
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:52,160
So who are you and what's your angle?

173
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:55,200
Do you go around attacking people just for kicks?

174
00:09:55,200 --> 00:10:05,300
My angle, let me tell you a story.

175
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:12,540
Once upon a time, in a certain village, there lived people who had tremendous magic power.

176
00:10:12,540 --> 00:10:16,740
They were special, greatly loved by the mana of this world.

177
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:21,600
They could control weather at will and manipulate the minerals.

178
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,600
Their powers were truly godlike.

179
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:30,340
Indeed, those outside their village came to revere them as divine beings.

180
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:34,800
But then, the people's feelings began to change.

181
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:38,600
Their respect and admiration became fear and envy.

182
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:44,680
They slaughtered their gods in a cowardly surprise attack and stole their power.

183
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,320
What kind of story is that?

184
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:49,380
Who cares?

185
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:53,180
You planning to become a bard?

186
00:10:53,180 --> 00:11:00,540
Well, I've got a story of my own you might like to hear.

187
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:05,160
It was once a young man with a bright mind and a pure heart.

188
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:09,680
His father was a fisherman who sent him out to work the sea at a young age.

189
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:15,220
Then one day, his boat got wrecked.

190
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:19,280
Seriously?

191
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:23,500
He fell into the water and washed up on an unknown shore.

192
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,780
Who is this kid?

193
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:28,220
He's very impressive.

194
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:35,520
He looked and acted different than the people there, so we got the crap beat out of him a lot.

195
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:37,460
But that was okay.

196
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:44,560
Because he turned around to beat the crap out of them and then became a badass squad boss.

197
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:45,640
The end.

198
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:53,640
Well, I think it's a pretty good story.

199
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:56,600
Of course, it is half my life, so there's that.

200
00:11:56,820 --> 00:11:57,220
Silence!

201
00:11:57,460 --> 00:11:59,120
How dare you, Mark Master Licht!

202
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,220
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

203
00:12:00,340 --> 00:12:02,380
That is one seriously freaky face!

204
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:04,580
What are those weird-looking lines for?

205
00:12:04,620 --> 00:12:06,120
Now's not really the time!

206
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:09,760
He's gotten faster.

207
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:14,300
If you're truly a foreigner, then my tale has nothing to do with you.

208
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:16,880
In which case, feel free to leave.

209
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:22,740
Captain Yami!

210
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:27,500
You've avoided mortal blows, but how much longer will your luck hold?

211
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:32,620
Are you the guy who messed up Wigolion so bad, huh?

212
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:35,700
That's right.

213
00:12:37,220 --> 00:12:42,360
I prepared so very carefully, and he walked right into my trap.

214
00:12:43,820 --> 00:12:45,020
Figured as much.

215
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:48,380
These little darts wouldn't do anything to a guy like him.

216
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:50,160
He'd take you down.

217
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:56,140
You've done that.

218
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:05,500
I'll just cover it in a distance.

219
00:13:05,940 --> 00:13:08,460
Game by moderates of Wigolion.

220
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:10,820
Let's do something.

221
00:13:10,820 --> 00:13:12,360
We'll see.

222
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:14,740
This little monsters have for us.

223
00:13:14,820 --> 00:13:15,500
Oh, no.

224
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:16,200
Wigolion.

225
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:17,260
Let's do something.

226
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:17,800
Hakes!

227
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:17,940
What?

228
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:47,920
Now dark magic, dark cloaks.

229
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:51,200
Lightless Slash!

230
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:54,460
Master Litt!

231
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:59,020
That was amazing! I've never seen anything like it before!

232
00:13:59,620 --> 00:14:03,780
Of course you used a trap. You couldn't win unless you played dirty.

233
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:04,900
Who are you?

234
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:08,600
Stop dancing around and come at me head on.

235
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:13,460
I'll show you what a squad captain can do. Think you can handle it?

236
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:18,940
Master Litt!

237
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:25,720
Hey kid, were you watching?

238
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,500
Uh, yes sir!

239
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:30,440
That's good, because now it's your turn.

240
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:31,120
Yes sir!

241
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:35,600
Wait, what did you say? There's no way I can do that!

242
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:38,380
Yeah? Last I checked, I was still your captain.

243
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:46,100
Which means if I tell you to do something, you do it. Assuming you want to be a real man someday, Shrimpster.

244
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:48,160
Please sir, that really hurts!

245
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:52,580
He blocked Master Litt's attacks, and even managed to fight back.

246
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:59,720
The captain of the Black Bulls. Could his power possibly rival the Wizard King's?

247
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:04,980
Hmph. Fascinating. The power of dark magic.

248
00:15:06,980 --> 00:15:10,720
Now, light recovery magic. Healing light particles.

249
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:17,280
Come on! Really? He can use recovery magic too?

250
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:19,400
I haven't seen it much myself.

251
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:24,540
But apparently, some people who've got a lot of mana can wield all kinds of different magic.

252
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:28,880
It's especially rare for attack types like him to be able to heal too.

253
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:32,820
Never mind that for now. You ready to go?

254
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:34,400
He was serious?!

255
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:38,860
Please sir, this is impossible! I can't do what you just did!

256
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:41,200
You remember I can't use magic, right?

257
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:43,980
I'm not talking about that last attack, moron.

258
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:48,040
I'm in this move here where I block his stupid little lightning bolts, see?

259
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,720
How do I hit something if I don't even know it's there?

260
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:56,440
Guess I've got no choice. I'll explain it to you once. For 500 Yule.

261
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,180
He's charging me?!

262
00:15:58,180 --> 00:16:00,820
You wanna know how I've been able to respond to his attacks?

263
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:05,120
It's cause I've been picking up on something that the people back in my country call Ki.

264
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:08,340
Ki? You weren't sensing his mana?

265
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:09,320
Nope.

266
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:14,440
A person's glance. Their breathing. Their scent.

267
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:17,720
The way their muscles move. The hint of their presence.

268
00:16:18,140 --> 00:16:22,560
Taken together. All of that living energy people give off. That's called Ki.

269
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:27,900
All I've been doing is reading his Ki and using it to predict his moves.

270
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:31,100
You've never done anything like that before?

271
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:33,880
Actually, yeah.

272
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:42,200
That's my fighting style. I combine the ability to sense Ki with my magic and the strength of my muscles.

273
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:46,040
Think of it as me being a buff magical swordsman.

274
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:50,160
You're not kidding about the buff part. Your neck's as thick as a tree.

275
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:52,600
Huh. Have you seen your neck lately?

276
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:58,580
Insolent. Carrying on a conversation mid-battle. Do they think we're fools?

277
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:04,440
That captain certainly is a mystery. He's surprisingly quick for someone who looks so sloppy.

278
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:13,780
He cannot be permitted to show you any further disrespect, Master. Please pardon my impertinence, but if I may step in...

279
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:21,060
Much appreciated, Valtos. You're always so eager to be of use. All right. The boy, perhaps.

280
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:25,860
Would you capture him for me? I don't mind if you need to hurt him a bit.

281
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:29,720
What? It would be my pleasure, Master.

282
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,760
That was close!

283
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:43,260
Hey, good timing. Practice on the evil scarecrow over there.

284
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:49,280
What? You want me to take on that guy? We talked about this! There's no way I'll be able to...

285
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:56,300
There's a saying where I'm from. Whatever happens, a warrior never goes back on his word.

286
00:17:57,180 --> 00:18:00,040
You did say you were going to be the Wizard King, right?

287
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:07,540
This is where you've got to push past your limits. If you don't, then your path ends here.

288
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:11,440
Yes, sir!

289
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:20,300
I have no idea what I'm supposed to do. So I'll just concentrate. Concentrate.

290
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:27,780
You truly think you'll be able to detect my attacks? An idiot boy who can use magic.

291
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:31,680
There it is!

292
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:35,920
I guess I missed some.

293
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:43,700
Nice try. You think I wouldn't notice you using just one of your senses? The only things you had work in there were your ears.

294
00:18:44,220 --> 00:18:50,200
That isn't reading, Ki. If you want to do this right, then you've got to feel it with your whole body. You got that?

295
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:51,820
My whole body?

296
00:18:51,820 --> 00:19:02,640
Yep. Don't rely only on your ears or just your eyes. It's like, uh, something in between intuition and prediction. Now do it right this time or I'll kill you.

297
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:04,000
This is insane!

298
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:19,140
Still, I think I kind of get it now. Not only my ears, not just my eyes. All right. I gotta reset everything. And concentrate.

299
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:28,960
Yes! There it is!

300
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,280
It worked!

301
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:47,700
Captain Yummy, did you see me?

302
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:52,300
Really? You actually managed to pull it off? No way. You're a freak.

303
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:52,740
What?

304
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:00,220
Valtos.

305
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:03,180
You hurt him.

306
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:05,220
How dare you?

307
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:12,720
I will not allow humans like you to continue harming my compatriots.

308
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:15,260
You've done too much damage already.

309
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:19,960
Jeez. What's this guy's problem? They're the ones who started all this?

310
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:20,400
Yeah.

311
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:27,740
As you can see, this particular spell traces an ever-changing track of whip-like undulations.

312
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:29,900
Can you anticipate these movements?

313
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:37,660
Long ago, when a person had sinned, the punishment was flogging.

314
00:20:38,020 --> 00:20:40,120
One popular instrument used was a whip.

315
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:43,500
I find this a very fitting in for the likes of you.

316
00:20:44,420 --> 00:20:45,740
Light creation magic.

317
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:47,740
Light whip of judgment.

318
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:56,740
Your struggles are pointless.

319
00:21:01,180 --> 00:21:02,260
It's crumbling!

320
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:06,720
That nutball's not holding anything back!

321
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:11,220
Aaaaaaah!

322
00:21:11,220 --> 00:21:11,720
Aaaaaaah!

323
00:21:11,720 --> 00:21:12,280
Aaaaaaah!

324
